    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="236" ed="#liebermann"/>Et rex suadet et mandat episcopis suis et comitibus et aldremannis et prepositis omnibus, ut curam adhibeant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IVAtr_8.lnote.oe.11"/> de illis qui tale falsum operantur et portant per patriam, sicut premissum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IVAtr_8.lnote.oe.12"/> est, utrobique cum Danis et Anglis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="8" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="76" ed="#robertson"/>Et rex suadet et mandat episcopis suis et comitibus et aldremannis et praepositis omnibus, ut curam adhibeant<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IVAtr_8.robnote.fn.12"/> de illis qui tale falsum operantur et portant per patriam, sicut praemissum<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IVAtr_8.robnote.fn.13"/> est, utrobique cum Danis et Anglis.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="237" ed="#liebermann"/>Und der König empfiehlt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_8.lnote.de.1"/> und gebietet seinen Bischöfen und Earls<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_8.lnote.de.2"/> und Ealdormen und allen Vögten, dass sie überall bei Dänen und Engländern auf jene Acht haben, welche solch falsches [Geld] herstellen und durchs Land bringen, wie oben gesagt ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And the king urges and commands his bishops and earls and ealdormen and all reeves that they keep watch everywhere, among Danes and English, on those who make such false [money] and bring it through the country, as was said above.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="77" ed="#robertson"/>And the king advises and commands his bishops and earls and ealdormen<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_8.robnote.n.1"/> and all his reeves that, both<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_8.robnote.n.2"/> among the Danes and the English<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IVAtr_8.robnote.n.3"/>, they be on the watch for those who coin such base money and spread it abroad through the country, as has been stated above.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="237"><ref target="clause:IVAtr_5">IV Atr 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. 5</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares IV Atr 5.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_8.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">236</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-at <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-at R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_8.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">236</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">prom. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">prom. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_8.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">ge</hi>)<hi rend="italic">rædeð</hi> ⁊ (<hi rend="italic">ge</hi>)<hi rend="italic">beodeð</hi> las wohl Original</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The original probably read (<hi rend="italic">ge</hi>)<hi rend="italic">rædeð</hi> ⁊ (<hi rend="italic">ge</hi>)<hi rend="italic">beodeð</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_8.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wenn nicht etwa <hi rend="italic">comitibus</hi> Glosse zu <hi rend="italic">ealdormannum</hi> war, las Original <hi rend="italic">eorlum</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">ealdormannum</hi>; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8h. 9.—In folg. Z. bessere statt ‘überall’: ‘bei beiden Parteien (Volksteilen)’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Unless <hi rend="italic">comitibus</hi> was a gloss on <hi rend="italic">ealdormannum</hi>, the original read <hi rend="italic">eorlum</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">ealdormannum</hi>; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8h. 9.—In the following line, for ‘everywhere’ read: ‘among both parties (sections of the people)’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_8.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dänen (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 13. 18) gehen voran</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Danes (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 13. 18) come first</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_8.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Probably tautological, though <hi rend="italic">comitibus</hi> may be a translation of <hi rend="italic">eorlum</hi> referring to Danish governors.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_8.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">utrobique</hi> etc. It is uncertain whether this phrase should be taken with <hi rend="italic">curam adhibeant</hi> or with <hi rend="italic">portant per patriam</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_8.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">326</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The order is noticeable.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_8.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>adhibeant</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">-eat</hi> R.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_8.robnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>praemissum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">prom.</hi> R, T.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
